<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mamluk Sultanate</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mamluk Sultanate was a state ruled by mamluk soldier elites in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> from 1250 to 1517. It replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a> and defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a> in 1260, halting their advance. It was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> in 1516 to 1517.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate.jpg" alt="Mamluk Sultanate" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mamluk_Sultanate_of_Cairo_1317_AD.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
